<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The pinned Node runtime in Contents/Helpers/node, which runs the helper under the hardened runtime (build-app.sh).

  Granted:
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit: V8 compiles JavaScript, and the WebAssembly of the QuickJS sandbox, into MAP_JIT
    memory, which the hardened runtime refuses without this.

  Not granted, though Node's own build has them (codesign -d entitlements of node v26.5.0):
  - allow-unsigned-executable-memory, disable-executable-page-protection: expected unneeded on Apple silicon, where V8
    uses MAP_JIT.
  - disable-library-validation: no native addon ships; QuickJS is WebAssembly.
  - allow-dyld-environment-variables: Caret builds the helper's environment itself and passes no DYLD_ variable.
  - get-task-allow: lets other processes attach a debugger.

  Evidence: none yet that allow-jit is needed, or enough. SIP is disabled on the Mac this was set up on
  (csrutil status, 2026-10-04), so the hardened runtime was not enforced, and the H4 probe saw every set pass,
  including no entitlements at all. Check on a Mac with SIP on before shipping: the helper must start and
  helper/test/codemode must pass with exactly this set.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
